  "body": "Part of #1446. The 2D Adaptive operation has the rest machining group in the model, the project file and MCP (branch `issue/1446-rest-adaptive-op`). The 2D Adaptive page has no rows for it.\n\nWhat is missing: a user cannot turn rest machining on for a 2D Adaptive in the app. Today the page keeps the value of the draft and does not show it.\n\nWanted: a \"Rest machining\" group on the `Passes` tab of the 2D Adaptive page.\n\n- An on/off switch. Off is the default. On seeds `source: PreviousOperations` and an allowance of 0.\n- One row, \"Rest allowance\".\n- No \"Rest stock from\" row and no previous tool rows: the 2D Adaptive reads the previous operations only.\n- A line that says where the stock comes from: the earlier operations of the same setup, which must be generated first.\n- The refusal texts of `operation::rest_op` shown before Apply when they apply: `REST_ADAPTIVE_TROCHOIDAL`, `REST_ADAPTIVE_ARC_TURNS`, `REST_ADAPTIVE_TILTED`.\n- The edit goes through `EditOperationParams`, as the other rows of the page do.\n\nPattern to follow: `crates/ui/src/egui_app/rest_pocket_page.rs` (#1815) and its tests `rest_pocket_tests.rs`.\n\nDone means:\n\n- The group is on the page and its tests assert labels, roles and the enabled state.\n- Apply writes the group, and undo restores the previous value.\n- The layout test of the page is updated.\n- The PR has before and after screenshots.\n",
